1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:05,496
For this lab, two paths in the synthetic
repository each validate an order

2
00:00:05,496 --> 00:00:06,123
quantity.

3
00:00:06,303 --> 00:00:11,902
The issue asks us to centralize that rule
while preserving both existing interfaces.

4
00:00:12,082 --> 00:00:17,615
Before opening the approved agent session
in GCP, identify the parts of this work

5
00:00:17,615 --> 00:00:18,844
that are in scope.

6
00:00:19,024 --> 00:00:23,513
Our boundary is the shared rule, two
callers, and their existing tests.

7
00:00:24,965 --> 00:00:29,966
Begin with a clean training branch and run
the existing tests in the authorized

8
00:00:29,966 --> 00:00:30,726
environment.

9
00:00:30,906 --> 00:00:35,886
Confirm that both callers have a positive
case and a zero or negative case.

10
00:00:36,066 --> 00:00:38,394
Save the result with the starting commit.

11
00:00:38,574 --> 00:00:43,918
A known baseline gives you a concrete way
to detect an unintended change once the

12
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:45,304
agent begins editing.

13
00:00:46,757 --> 00:00:51,818
In an approved agent client, ask for a
plan with an explicit stop after each

14
00:00:51,818 --> 00:00:52,217
stage.

15
00:00:52,397 --> 00:00:56,845
Have the agent identify the actual call
sites and the tests it will run.

16
00:00:57,025 --> 00:01:01,015
Open the referenced files and check that
the plan fits the issue.

17
00:01:01,195 --> 00:01:06,402
Once you approve the first stage, keep the
second stage pending until the first stage

18
00:01:06,402 --> 00:01:07,137
is verified.

19
00:01:08,590 --> 00:01:12,429
After the first stage, review the diff in
the affected files.

20
00:01:12,609 --> 00:01:17,584
Look at the comparison itself, the public
behavior of the command, and the tests

21
00:01:17,584 --> 00:01:19,512
that demonstrate compatibility.

22
00:01:19,692 --> 00:01:24,435
If the agent proposes the focused test
command, confirm that it is the approved

23
00:01:24,435 --> 00:01:25,996
command for this checkout.

24
00:01:26,176 --> 00:01:29,527
Keep the proof from this run before asking
it to proceed.

25
00:01:31,007 --> 00:01:36,105
During the second stage, the example agent
proposes touching a deployment file.

26
00:01:36,285 --> 00:01:40,660
The issue needs an API caller change and a
check of its behavior.

27
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:43,403
Pause before accepting the proposed edit.

28
00:01:43,583 --> 00:01:48,095
Point the agent at the approved files
again and ask for a revised plan.

29
00:01:48,275 --> 00:01:52,393
Record the decision so the reviewer can
see why the change stayed small.

30
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:58,571
When the second diff is ready, check the
list of changed files as well as the

31
00:01:58,571 --> 00:01:59,493
actual changes.

32
00:01:59,673 --> 00:02:04,960
Run the same baseline suite, and confirm
the original cases still hold for both

33
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:05,496
callers.

34
00:02:05,676 --> 00:02:09,154
Make sure the test result belongs to the
current revision.

35
00:02:09,334 --> 00:02:14,496
A pass from an earlier stage only proves
the code that existed at that stage.

36
00:02:15,965 --> 00:02:21,506
Summarize the behavior preserved, the code
paths changed, and the baseline and final

37
00:02:21,506 --> 00:02:22,363
test results.

38
00:02:22,543 --> 00:02:25,789
Keep the final diff available for the
author to review.

39
00:02:25,969 --> 00:02:31,145
The separate reviewer checks the pull
request and its evidence from the approved

40
00:02:31,145 --> 00:02:32,762
terminal with GitHub CLI.

41
00:02:32,942 --> 00:02:37,871
This approach scales because each stage
leaves evidence that another person can

42
00:02:37,871 --> 00:02:38,370
inspect.

43
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:42,998
Try the same method on another training
refactor.

44
00:02:43,178 --> 00:02:48,362
Pick an existing behavior, identify two
short stages and give each stage a

45
00:02:48,362 --> 00:02:49,833
verification command.

46
00:02:50,013 --> 00:02:55,435
Notice which decisions the agent can make
within the task and which decisions belong

47
00:02:55,435 --> 00:02:56,209
to a person.

48
00:02:56,389 --> 00:03:01,406
The most useful checkpoint is the one that
catches a mistake while the diff is still

49
00:03:01,406 --> 00:03:01,765
small.
